# Copy to `.env.local` when you need a local override. Nothing here is required for
# development: with both variables unset the client calls `/api`, which Vite proxies to
# `http://localhost:5200` (see `server.proxy` in `vite.config.ts`).

# Backend API base URL. Unset (the default for local work) means `/api`, i.e. the dev
# proxy. A build without this falls back to `/api` as well, so it is only set for a
# deployment that serves the API somewhere else.
# VITE_API_URL=https://fms-api-3ba95327d590.herokuapp.com/api

# WARNING: Vite loads `.env.local` in EVERY mode and it takes precedence over
# `.env.production`. A `VITE_API_URL` left in `.env.local` silently points local
# development — and any build made on this machine — at whatever it names, bypassing the
# proxy. That is how local dev ended up CORS-blocked against the deployed API. Keep
# `.env.local` free of `VITE_API_URL` unless you are deliberately testing against another
# host, and comment that line out when you are done.
